            "created_at": "2025-08-28T09:57:37.847619+00:00",
            "notes": "[Launch Vector](item_7d4ef8eb-a008-4f63-802d-a67bd9d6989e) Launch Vector will consistently do more damage in Rounds 1-3 than Speed Kills, especially around grouped enemies. Get a Power Playbook to compliment it.\n\n\nPharah is in danger the moment Cassidy, Soldier 76 or even a slight breeze heads her way. Buy two survival items and laugh straight to the bank.\n\nRound 1:\n [Plasma Converter](item_25869f9a-9a29-4e19-96b6-9d8a28c59318) \n [Armored Vest](item_358361e2-59be-4c81-b221-8a87f37809e6) \n [Electrolytes](item_274b7523-8273-4740-aa7b-837f3f143900)\n\nAlternatives:\n [Charged Plating](item_b8ca58e7-6ae2-40ee-8618-fe2f32315295) \n [Adrenaline Shot](item_ab8eba6a-0bda-4b12-8854-4ba4169b515f) \n\nNerd Breakdown:\n\nCompensator takes our rocket damage from 120 to ~126 on a target without armor/damage reduction. Power Playbook takes our Concussive blast from ~110 (on a single target with all mini rockets) to ~121, which also affects multiple enemies. Weapon Grease doesn't have much impact on our damage this early (taking about 10-12 rockets before the damage scales beyond the base). Early high burst damage and being able to live is our goal. \n\nArmored Vest + Electrolytes offers you the safest sustained choice. Adrenaline Shot over Armored Vest can also be considered if you are familiar with health pack spawns and lack of projectiles on the enemy team (Armored Vest will always be great against Reaper, Soldier, Dva, Orisa, Junker Queen,",
